            <ArticleTitle>Large sinus of Valsalva aneurysm causing myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0218492311421454</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 41-year-old man was urgently admitted with sudden onset of chest pain. Emergency coronary angiography revealed a large aneurysm of the sinus of Valsalva and reduced blood flow in the left coronary artery. A modified Bentall operation and coronary artery bypass were performed successfully. A large sinus of Valsalva aneurysm should be regarded as a critical problem that could cause coronary insufficiency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
